    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25475" root="ضبح" body-key="D">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَابِحٌ</span></b>  A man <i>raising his voice in reading</i> or
<i>reciting:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَوَابِحُ</span>, which is anomalous, like
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَوَارِسُ</span> [pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَارِسٌ</span>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَيْلٌ ضَوَابِحُ</span>
<i>Horses stretching forth their arms in their going
along:</i> (A:) or <i>running vehemently;</i> like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَوَابِعُ</span>.
(TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضبع</span>.)

